updated: '2026-10-14'
---

`.rivet.local.json` holds per-project task settings. `:RivetRunOptions` edits the JSON and previews it before saving. Generated projects ignore this file; add an ignore rule in an existing project if needed.

```json
{
  "args": ["--input", "data/example with spaces.bin"],
  "cwd": ".",
  "env": { "MODE": "experiment" },
  "jobs": 8,
  "threads": 4
}
```

## Available fields

| Field | Type and effect |
| --- | --- |
| `args` | String array appended to Run, Benchmark, or Profile argv. |
| `cwd` | Project-relative directory for Run, Benchmark, and Profile; defaults to the root. Other tasks use the root. |
| `env` | Object of string environment values applied to task processes. |
| `jobs` | Positive integer for CMake/Cargo/Swift build concurrency. |
| `threads` | Positive integer setting `OMP_NUM_THREADS`, overriding that key in `env`. |
| `ranks`, `gpus` | Positive integer hook parameters; setting them alone allocates no resources. |
| `launcher` | Argv prefix for Run, such as `["mpiexec", "-n", "{ranks}"]`. |
| `benchmark`, `profile` | Command arrays; the workflow configures and builds before executing the hook. |
| `submit`, `status`, `cancel` | Command arrays; run without an implicit build or polling. |
| `job_id` | Scheduler ID string for status/cancel hooks. |
| `python` | Python interpreter override. |
| `python_module` | Python module to run with `-m`. |
| `test_runner` | `unittest` (default) or `pytest` for Python. |
| `lua` | Executable override compatible with the project's Lua, LuaJIT, or Neovim runtime. |

Arguments are individual strings; Rivet does not evaluate shell syntax. Keep secrets in the inherited environment when they should not appear in settings or command output. Optional tools must already be installed.

## Hook placeholders

Launcher and hook command arrays expand `{root}`, `{executable}`, `{ranks}`, `{threads}`, `{gpus}`, and `{job_id}`. Placeholder expansion does not apply to `args`, `env`, or `cwd`.

Unset resource placeholders expand to `1`; using `{job_id}` requires `job_id`. For Benchmark/Profile, `{executable}` resolves the selected CMake artifact, Cargo build artifact, or SwiftPM executable. Python and Lua hooks should specify their interpreter and script/module command explicitly.

## Benchmark and profiler commands

```json
{
  "benchmark": ["hyperfine", "--shell=none", "{executable}"],
  "profile": ["nsys", "profile", "--output", "profile-run", "{executable}"]
}
```

This benchmark example assumes an executable path without spaces and no shared `args`. Hyperfine expects each measured command as one string: quote paths and include application arguments inside that string according to its [command syntax](https://github.com/sharkdp/hyperfine/blob/master/doc/hyperfine.1). Rivet appends shared `args` to Hyperfine itself, which does not forward them as application arguments. The [Nsight Systems command](https://docs.nvidia.com/nsight-systems/UserGuide/index.html) accepts application arguments after the executable.

Select `:RivetTask benchmark` or `:RivetTask profile` to run the configured hook.

## Slurm examples

```json
{
  "ranks": 4,
  "threads": 2,
  "gpus": 1,
  "submit": ["sbatch", "--parsable", "--ntasks", "{ranks}", "--cpus-per-task", "{threads}", "--gpus", "{gpus}", "jobs/run.sbatch"],
  "status": ["squeue", "--jobs", "{job_id}"],
  "cancel": ["scancel", "{job_id}"],
  "job_id": "12345"
}
```

Supply your batch script and site-specific account, partition, and GPU settings. Run `:RivetTask submit`, then replace the example `job_id` with the returned job ID before selecting Status or Cancel. Rivet does not capture the ID or poll automatically. See the [Slurm batch reference](https://slurm.schedmd.com/sbatch.html).

In the Neovim task output buffer, Ctrl-C terminates the local process group: TERM first, then KILL after one second on macOS/Linux. Children that create a separate session are outside that group. A scheduler job already accepted remotely needs the explicit Cancel hook.
